that ever assembled at any one place at any one time in the history of America to do homage to God, the flag and the home. So stirring stuff there in the newspaper, The Fiery Cross, which was public, in Indianapolis on the 13th of July 1923, and it's describing an enormous Independence Day picnic. And I'm guessing, Dominic, from the name of that newspaper, The Fiery Cross, that the Ku Klux Klan may have something to do with this. Yeah, you're not wrong, Tom.

